From: Christophe (fork iwrt-2512) <noreply@localhost>
Date: Wed, 10 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_ppe: add missing prototype for mtk_ppe_cache_clear()

999-3013 renders mtk_ppe_cache_clear() global but declares no prototype
in mtk_ppe.h, which triggers -Wmissing-prototypes (enabled by default
since Linux 6.8 via Makefile.extrawarn).

Keep the symbol global (in case 999-3019 adaptive-PPPQ is ever ported)
and add the declaration next to the other mtk_ppe_* prototypes.

Signed-off-by: Christophe (fork iwrt-2512)
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_ppe.h
@@ -356,6 +356,7 @@
 
 void mtk_ppe_deinit(struct mtk_eth *eth);
 void mtk_ppe_update_mtu(struct mtk_ppe *ppe, int mtu);
+void mtk_ppe_cache_clear(struct mtk_ppe *ppe);
 void mtk_ppe_start(struct mtk_ppe *ppe);
 int mtk_ppe_stop(struct mtk_ppe *ppe);
 int mtk_ppe_prepare_reset(struct mtk_ppe *ppe);
